{
  "id": "Compound::DB06770 - Gene::1571",
  "verbalization": "Benzyl Alcohol is shown to interact with Cyp2b6 and Cyp2d6, both of which are involved in the metabolism of arachidonic acid. These enzymes are part of the cytochrome P450 family and are known to catalyze the epoxidation of arachidonic acid, a critical step in the biosynthesis of pro-inflammatory lipid mediators. The observed interaction between Benzyl Alcohol and these enzymes suggests a potential mechanism by which the compound may influence the metabolic pathways leading to the production of inflammatory mediators. The shared involvement of Cyp2e1 in these processes, through its participation in arachidonic acid epoxidation, indicates a possible role for Benzyl Alcohol in modulating the activity of Cyp2e1. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust, biologically plausible relationship, though further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the direct impact of Benzyl Alcohol on Cyp2e1 function.",
